### ReWave network — media library (video pool, ad-break ingestion).
### Variable sources: requests/http-client.env.json (JetBrains) or .vscode/settings.json (VS Code REST Client).
### Bodies are copies of the example objects in openapi.yaml — keep them in sync.

### List the media pool — GET /v1/videos (scope: videos:read)
# Expected: 200 with VideoList (one processed and one pending video in the
# openapi example); 501 while stubbed
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/videos

### List only processed videos — GET /v1/videos?processed=true (scope: videos:read)
# Expected: 200, videos filtered by ingestion state; 501 while stubbed
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/videos?processed=true

### Add a video — POST /v1/videos (scope: videos:write)
# Triggers ad-break ingestion asynchronously; the response has processed=false —
# poll the video detail to watch the ad-break points fill in.
# Expected: 201, Location: /v1/videos/{id}, body: Video with processed=false;
# 409 if the path already exists; 501 while stubbed
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/videos HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "path": "/media-pool/movies/new-movie.mp4",
  "title": "New Movie",
  "tags": [
    "movie"
  ]
}

### Video detail — GET /v1/videos/{videoId} (scope: videos:read)
# Expected: 200 with Video including detected adBreaks; 404 unknown id;
# 501 while stubbed
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/videos/{{videoId}}

### Remove a video — DELETE /v1/videos/{videoId} (scope: videos:write)
# Removes the video and its ad-break points; already resolved playlists are
# not rewritten.
# Expected: 204; 404 unknown id; 501 while stubbed
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/videos/{{videoId}}
